== o2_mechanisms ==

-- A12: A1-A2, all 24 bijections of {(z, x)}, z visible, x hidden
   induced visible channels (rows: input z; entries P(z'|z)), with the hidden x fresh and uniform:
     ((Fraction(0, 1), Fraction(1, 1)), (Fraction(1, 1), Fraction(0, 1)))  [flip]  x4
     ((Fraction(1, 2), Fraction(1, 2)), (Fraction(1, 2), Fraction(1, 2)))  [replace by uniform]  x16
     ((Fraction(1, 1), Fraction(0, 1)), (Fraction(0, 1), Fraction(1, 1)))  [identity]  x4
A12a     PASS  all 24 induced channels are DC and lie in {identity, flip, replace by uniform} (3 distinct)
A12b     PASS  composite sandwich, 24 x 24 x 2 seeds: V_max = 0
   => A12: input non-monomial = False; readout = passive; V_max = 0; induced visible operation: identity / flip / replace by uniform (classical); class: FAILED-ENVELOPE

-- A36: link-coupled, centre-independent, linear second-order rule on a ring (N=3, K=2, q=2)
A36a     PASS  the rule is a bijection of the 4096 configurations
A36b     PASS  A5 linearity over F_2: phi(s) = sum of phi on basis vectors, for all 4096 states
A36c     PASS  A6 gauge covariance: phi_{G M G^-1}(G s) = G phi_M(s), three gauge fields, all states
A36d     PASS  passive sandwich (two rule steps): P_coh(0) = 1/2, P_deph(0) = 1/2; one step P(0|0) = 1/2 (the rule is a permutation of configurations, so O1-T3 applies on the matrix carrier)
   => A36: input non-monomial = False; readout = passive; V_max = 0; induced visible operation: classical stochastic, P(z1=0|z0=0) = 1/2; class: FAILED-ENVELOPE

